From: Onur Bingol <obingol@anaconda.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 10:42:46 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Keep libpython linked to executables on Linux under -Wl,--as-needed

Linux equivalent of link_python_to_executables.patch's existing -needed_library
fix for macOS, which counters conda-forge's -dead_strip_dylibs the same way
this counters conda-forge's -Wl,--as-needed. Executables that transitively
link "python" (e.g. testJsIO, via tf) but reference no Python symbol of their
own get libpython dropped by --as-needed, so GNU ld fails the link with
"undefined reference" to CPython C API symbols left unresolved in
usd_tf.so/usd_python.so by PXR_PY_UNDEFINED_DYNAMIC_LOOKUP (macOS instead
fails at runtime, not link time, which is why the Apple fix alone wasn't
enough here). --no-as-needed disables that pruning for such executables. See
https://github.com/PixarAnimationStudios/OpenUSD/issues/2371 and
https://github.com/PixarAnimationStudios/OpenUSD/issues/2568 for background.

diff --git a/pxr/external/boost/python/CMakeLists.txt b/pxr/external/boost/python/CMakeLists.txt
index 8f2466b..3333333 100644
--- a/pxr/external/boost/python/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/pxr/external/boost/python/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -364,6 +364,24 @@ if (PXR_PY_UNDEFINED_DYNAMIC_LOOKUP)
     if(APPLE)
         set_property(TARGET python APPEND PROPERTY INTERFACE_LINK_OPTIONS
             "$<$<STREQUAL:$<TARGET_PROPERTY:TYPE>,EXECUTABLE>:LINKER:-needed_library,$<TARGET_FILE:Python3::Python>>"
+        )
+    endif()
+    # Anaconda: conda-forge's Linux LDFLAGS include -Wl,--as-needed, which is
+    # the ELF analogue of the macOS -dead_strip_dylibs problem handled above:
+    # an executable that doesn't reference a Python symbol directly has no
+    # "need" of its own for libpython, so --as-needed drops its DT_NEEDED
+    # entry. Unlike on macOS, where symbol resolution for an already-built
+    # .dylib always succeeds lazily at load time regardless of --as-needed,
+    # GNU ld additionally requires -- when creating an EXECUTABLE -- that
+    # every undefined symbol carried by usd_tf.so/usd_python.so (left
+    # unresolved there on purpose by PXR_PY_UNDEFINED_DYNAMIC_LOOKUP) be
+    # resolved from something explicitly on the link line, and silently
+    # dropping libpython defeats that, producing "undefined reference" to
+    # CPython C API symbols at static link time instead of a runtime crash.
+    # --no-as-needed disables that pruning so libpython is always kept.
+    if(UNIX AND NOT APPLE)
+        set_property(TARGET python APPEND PROPERTY INTERFACE_LINK_OPTIONS
+            "$<$<STREQUAL:$<TARGET_PROPERTY:TYPE>,EXECUTABLE>:LINKER:--no-as-needed>"
         )
     endif()
 endif()
